                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "\"Hello developers! I’m a player from China. Many years ago, I used to play your Tank Blitz on the 4399 mini-games website. Back then, it was considered one of the highest-quality games in the tank category. Since I didn't know English at the time, I didn't know how to continue after beating it. Later, I found out it was just a beta version.\n\nRecently, I thought of your game again and searched for it, only to discover it’s now on Steam! I immediately came here to show my support. It’s honestly so heartwarming and nostalgic to see your game here, especially since so many other fun mini-games never got any follow-up. The era of Flash mini-games has truly passed, but I believe a lot of kids in China probably played your beta version on those flash game sites back in the day.\n\nBy the way, it seems like no one on Chinese video platforms has posted gameplay videos of your game lately, so I decided to help spread the word, haha! I also noticed that your game was released on Steam back in 2017, but there was basically no news about it here, and most of the reviews are from that year. I was wondering, has development for this game officially stopped? Are you currently working on any new games, or what have you been up to lately? (Just asking out of curiosity, no pressure to answer at all!)\n\nNowadays, I also want to become a game developer. Making games is genuinely such a joyful experience. Time really flies—it feels like I’m having a conversation across time and space...\n\nP.S. I typed this out and used a browser to translate it, so please forgive me if there are any mistakes!\"\n",
